amming gate, fingers white on the strap of her bag.'' Want: protect sibling; trait: protective resolve; detail: white-knuckled strap can return later. Think about how this word or relationship creates meaning.\n\nTRY FIRST\nUnderline or quote one precise detail in the model and explain its effect.\n\nFEEDBACK\nThe most useful evidence is a specific choice in the example, followed by an explanation of the effect on meaning.","explain":"Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does for a reader.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make decisions based on specific language evidence, rather than guess or copy someone else. Keep the meaning accurate and explain the choice.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the original example and locate the words or actions that support the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Check your response against the feedback: did you address the same skill and show your reasoning? If a detail is uncertain, identify what would have to be checked. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than making the answer longer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Saying a choice is good without naming the actual detail does not show understanding. Correct the meaning, not just the appearance.","title":"Explain the evidence","visual":[{"alt":"Consistent detail.","caption":"Thread continuity.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Detail</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">white-knuckle strap</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Return</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">later scene echo</text></g></svg>"}]},{"check":{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Use an intentio